{
  "_about": "Channels the guide opens in their official app. ZEE5 links open the live channel in ZEE5's player; JioHotstar links open the channel's page (latest episodes; Star Sports pages carry the live match). Read from the services' public live-TV and channel pages on 2026-11-03. Sony LIV dropped live TV in 2023, so it has none. An app's \"package\" can list several builds (ZEE5 is com.graymatrix.did on Google Play, com.zee5.amazon on the Fire TV); the guide uses whichever is installed. \"live\": the link plays the channel; \"player\": part of the app's player screen name for one-EXIT return; \"optional\": only offered where installed. Apps are tried in the order listed here. JioTV+ (Fire TV, Jio account): jiotvplus://open.classicplayer?cid=<content id> plays the channel live when JioTV+ is set to Classic TV (its Settings); the app:// form of the same link only resumes the last channel. Content ids come from JioTV+'s own search provider (the guide's jiotvplus_lookup extra, see JioTvPlusLookup.java), read 2026-11-03; the guide looks them up again by itself when JioTV+ is updated or a week has passed (a row's optional 6th field is JioTV+'s own name for the channel, searched instead of ours). JioTV+'s search did not return Star Pravah, Star Jalsha, Star Vijay, Asianet or Star Utsav, so those keep only their JioHotstar page. Zee's channels open in ZEE5 only (the owner's choice), so JioTV+ rows are not made for them. ZEE5's free live channels need Google's video-ad loader imasdk.googleapis.com, which the Fire TV's NextDNS blocked until the owner allowlisted it (2026-11-03); ZEE5 also has to be signed in. Zee Café HD was dropped on 2026-11-04 (owner): the channel closed on 1 June 2026 (replaced by Unite8 Sports 1) and its ZEE5 page gives error AUB-GET-404-1002. &flix HD was dropped the same day (owner: it does not open; same ZEE5 error; turned into a sports channel with Zee Café in 2026), and &Privé HD too (owner: ZEE5 opens but does not play it; same ZEE5 error). Star World was dropped on 2026-11-08 (owner: it opened JioHotstar's home page): the channel closed in India on 15 March 2023. Tested on the Fire TV the same day: JioHotstar's TV app (26.10.26) opens none of its channel or show pages from a link (it shows Who's watching? or nothing, then its home page; hotstar:// forms and a search request too); only some live watch links play. So Star Sports 1 and Star Sports 2 open JioTV+'s HD channels live first (no SD in JioTV+; the 6th field is the HD name for the lookup), keeping their JioHotstar page as the fallback elsewhere.",
